diff --git a/docs/development.md b/docs/development.md
index 0bca076..2127fa5 100644
--- a/docs/development.md
+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -72,6 +72,12 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Languages
+
+Fizzy speaks English and Japanese (see `config.i18n.available_locales`). Open any page with `?locale=ja` to switch: the choice sticks to the browser session and, once signed in, to the identity, so it follows people to their next sign-in. Emails and push notifications are written in the recipient's language.
+
+Translations live in `config/locales/`: the general vocabulary in `en.yml`/`ja.yml`, everything else by area under `config/locales/en/` and `config/locales/ja/`. Views use lazy lookup (`t(".key")`), so a key's home is the template that renders it. Dates, numbers and validation messages come from the `rails-i18n` gem. Missing translations raise in the test environment, and the static error pages in `public/` are bilingual because they're served without knowing who is looking.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
